            <ArticleTitle>[Enzyme preparations in conservative treatment of chronic pancreatitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>86-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To study effectiveness of enzyme medicine pancitrate 25,000 in the treatment of chronic pancreatitis (CP).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Pain, stool, creato- and steatorea, other signs of CP were examined before and after pancitrate treatment of 17 patients with chronic pancreatitis aged from 28 to 62 years.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Pancitrate 25,000 reduced stomach pains in 16 of 17 patients. Stool returned to normal in 8 of 13 patients. Creato- and steatorea decreased.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">New dosage forms of the enzyme preparations (pancitrate 25,000, in particular) are highly effective both in deficiency of pancreatic external secretion and pain relief in exacerbation of CP.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
